  "body": "### What is the issue with the MIME Sniffing Standard?\n\nOn Firefox we recently got a webcompat report: [2006569 - ghosttogether.net - Change password page is not displayed, shows the html code instead](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2006569)\n\nThe page starts with `<!--scaffold.--><html>...` and has no content-type.\nAccording to https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#determining-the-computed-mime-type-of-a-resource sniffing `<!--` must be followed by ` ` or `>`.\nBut Chrome and Safari don't respect that, and I think for `<!--` we can relax the restriction of being followed by a tag terminating byte, since `<!--` would be a valid start to a HTML comment regardless of what follows.\n\nI'm changing Firefox's behaviour in [2011628 - Sniff !-- as HTML to match Chrome](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2011628) and also adding a tentative WPT.",
